            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for solemn, then the Russian for festive."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: поздравлять",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поздравлять (pozdravlyát) — \"to congratulate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Друзья поздравили меня с днём рождения. Druzyá pozdrávili menyá s dnyom rozhdéniya. My friends wished me a happy birthday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective поздравить (pozdrávit), поздравлю. The occasion takes с + instrumental: с праздником!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поздравлять (pozdravlyát) (EtymDB: \"to congratulate\") is built on по- and здравый \"healthy\", the Church Slavonic shape (EtymDB: Church Slavonic sŭdravŭ) of native здоровый: to wish someone health."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
